WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.663
Read the guide's Step 4.

2
00:00:01.663 --> 00:00:03.801
It sets six rules for this gate.

3
00:00:03.801 --> 00:00:06.025
One automatic policy per package.

4
00:00:06.025 --> 00:00:07.063
No member-of.

5
00:00:07.063 --> 00:00:11.762
A grace period for movers, so a move
doesn't cut someone off mid-handover.

6
00:00:11.762 --> 00:00:14.612
Manager approval, with
a fallback approver.

7
00:00:14.612 --> 00:00:17.013
The mover workflow's residual review.

8
00:00:17.013 --> 00:00:20.074
And privileged access kept
out of rules altogether.

9
00:00:20.074 --> 00:00:21.287
Why no member-of?

10
00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:24.578
From November 3, 2026,
Learn quarantines an

11
00:00:24.578 --> 00:00:28.338
automatic assignment
policy whose rule uses it.

12
00:00:28.338 --> 00:00:33.275
The policy stays, but it adds and removes
nothing until the operator is removed,

13
00:00:33.275 --> 00:00:37.149
and Learn publishes a read-only
script to find those policies.

14
00:00:37.149 --> 00:00:42.493
Then read the design in the Federal
Modernization Workbook's Book 03's Chapter 10:

15
00:00:42.493 --> 00:00:46.082
its rule patterns, access
packages and access reviews,

16
00:00:46.082 --> 00:00:48.475
and where dynamic membership stops.

17
00:00:48.475 --> 00:00:51.600
Its Chapter 08 says
what a move must start.
